# AutoVault Motors — public configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in only the values you have.
# Every value below is PUBLIC: it ships to the browser and must never contain
# an API key, password or private token. All three are optional — the site runs
# without them and degrades honestly (see the notes on each one).
#
# NOTE: the concept's own public contact details already ship in the committed
# `.env.production`, so a fresh Vercel/Netlify import works with no setup at
# all. Use `.env.local` to override them locally, and the host dashboard to
# override them in a real deployment.

# The dealership's WhatsApp number, in international format, digits only.
# Example: a Nigerian number written locally as 0801 234 5678 becomes:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=2348012345678
# Spaces, dashes, brackets and a leading + or 00 are tolerated.
# Leave empty to disable all WhatsApp actions; the interface then explains that
# no number is configured instead of linking to a made-up number.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=

# Optional public email address used by the contact form's mailto fallback and
# the footer. Leave empty to hide email everywhere.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# Optional public site URL, used for canonical links, Open Graph URLs, the
# sitemap and robots.txt. Must be the full origin with no trailing slash.
# Example: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://autovault.growthly.example
# Leave empty during development: no canonical tags or sitemap entries are
# emitted until a verified domain is supplied.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
